{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"8599b7763963d7f6cf470cb70d2655909d3e69fdfc58e82c3bc2246f0142ece5","digest":{"component_or_area":"reconciler read/check paths","key_entities":["src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/runtime.py","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_backend_registry.py","ReconcilerSettings","GitRuntime","BridgeRuntime","Jira Cloud","Jira Data Center","SecretStr","SecretBytes","reconcile-check","tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_operation_bindings.py","load_config()"],"problem_keywords":["reconciler","ambient config reload","immutable settings","read path stability","Jira backend","auth carrier","secrets handling","operation runtime"],"propositions":["Reconciler read/check paths call load_config() and inspect environment/cwd, allowing ambient settings to change read scope or discard supplied registry config during a single operation run.","Jira backend construction is not isolated to a single immutable composition, causing project/query scope, TLS, timeout/limits, and auth capability to reload from ambient sources rather than remain stable for the operation.","Secrets and auth carriers must be excluded from repr/equality/hash/cache/fingerprint and unwrapped only in the selected Jira sending adapter to prevent leakage across diagnostic boundaries.","Preflight, access check, fetch, paging, diff, mapper, sanitizer, property access, tracker/binding reads, and Git ref/layout owners must thread a single stable backend/runtime rather than perform independent ambient resolves."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787703934263196001,"uuid":"3893a364-